---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/app.css';
import '../styles/page.css';
---

<AppLayout
	title="About — doodleai.art"
	description="What doodleai.art is: sign in, chat with an agent, attach a photo, and get back a hand-drawn doodle avatar or collage using account credits."
>
	<Navbar />

	<main class="page">
		<div class="page-hero">
			<div class="eyebrow">About</div>
			<h1>A doodle booth you <span class="grad">chat</span> with</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				doodleai.art turns a photo into a hand-drawn doodle avatar or collage. Instead of a form,
				you talk to an agent: attach a photo (or just describe a character), say what you want, and
				it draws it.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="prose">
			<h2>The idea</h2>
			<p>
				Most "AI photo" tools are a picker full of filters. This one is a conversation — attach a
				photo, tell the agent what you're after, and it picks the right doodle style, generates it,
				and lets you keep refining ("thicker outline", "warmer paper") until it's right.
			</p>
			<p>
				<strong>Sign in to create.</strong> Your account keeps chats, saved doodles, and characters in sync
				across devices. Generation runs through Doodle AI's platform connection and account credits.
			</p>

			<h2>How it works</h2>
			<ol class="steps">
				<li><b>Sign in.</b> Google sign-in unlocks creation, syncing, and your starter credits.</li>
				<li><b>Start a chat.</b> Attach a photo, mention a saved character with @, or just describe someone for a surprise.</li>
				<li><b>The agent draws it.</b> It picks a skill — a single avatar, a close-up collage, a full-body action collage — and generates it.</li>
				<li><b>Keep it or refine it.</b> Ask for changes, remix, save to your moodboard, or download.</li>
			</ol>

			<h2>Platform-powered generation</h2>
			<p>
				Doodle AI handles the provider connection on the server, so you can focus on the creative part.
				Each generation uses account credits, with starter credits included for new accounts. Chat is
				routed through OpenRouter and images are processed by PicX.
			</p>

			<div class="facts">
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Login required</div>
					<div class="v">For creation</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Cost to use this site</div>
					<div class="v">Free</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Your synced workspace</div>
					<div class="v">Account-scoped</div>
				</div>
				<div class="fact">
					<div class="k">Skill needed</div>
					<div class="v">Zero</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<h2>What this isn't</h2>
			<p>
				There's no feed or public gallery. Your account-scoped chats, moodboard, saved characters, and
				generated results are visible only to you through the app. We don't build an advertising profile,
				and provider credentials are never exposed to your browser.
			</p>

			<h2>Who made this</h2>
			<p>
				doodleai.art is a small side project — built fast, deployed on Cloudflare's edge. It's
				the kind of thing that exists because it was fun enough to ship.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="page-cta">
			<a href="/">Start doodling →</a>
		</div>
	</main>

	<Footer />

	<script>
		import { initThemeToggle } from '../lib/theme';
		const themeToggle = document.getElementById('themeToggle');
		if (themeToggle) initThemeToggle(themeToggle);
	</script>
</AppLayout>
